<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

	<!-- Enrols the dust bunny in A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2).

	     ADS 2 does not name recipes one by one. It keeps three abstract RecipeDefs, ADS_Cat1 (medieval
	     replacements: peg legs, dentures), ADS_Cat2 (+ simple prosthetics) and ADS_Cat3 (+ bionics), and its
	     own last patch, Patches/z_Category_Patches.xml, copies their recipeUsers onto the real surgery bases
	     with PatchOperationAddOrMergeCopy. Adding an animal means adding one <li> to those lists.

	     CATEGORY 1 ONLY. ADS 2 labels its categories "1: basic replacements", "2: 1 + simple prosthetics" and
	     "3: 2 + bionics". Category 1 is the broadest list, every animal ADS 2 knows is in it, and the larger
	     and trainable ones are also listed in 2 and 3. A dust bunny is trainable, but it is a clump of lint
	     of body size 0.04 in play: a peg leg or a denture is a joke that works, a bionic arm on it is not.

	     ORDER MATTERS. The copy takes the list as it is at that instant, so an <li> added after it lands in
	     a list nobody reads any more. ADS 2's own compatibility patches are safe because file names sort
	     inside one mod; a patch in another mod is not. That is why About.xml says loadBefore
	     SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2: Verse.LoadedModManager.ApplyPatches runs the active mods in
	     load order, so this patch has to come first.

	     The guard is PatchOperationConditional on ADS_Cat1. Without ADS 2 the xpath selects nothing, no
	     <nomatch> is declared, and the operation reports success without a line in the log.

	     NOT MayRequire. MayRequire on an <Operation> is read by nothing: Verse.PatchOperation has no such
	     field and ModContentPack.LoadPatches never reads the attribute, so the operation would apply whether
	     ADS 2 is loaded or not. It is honoured on a def node, on a <li> and on an ordinary field element,
	     which is what makes the wrong form look like the right one. -->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>DustBunny</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
